    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">How to Sign a PDF on an iPhone</h1>

    <p>For a detailed breakdown of the pros and cons of mobile signing, read our full post: <a href="/blog/signing-on-iphone">How to Sign a PDF on an iPhone (The Fast Way)</a>.</p>

    <h2>Quick Summary: iOS Markup vs usignpdf</h2>

    <h3>Using iOS Markup (Good for casual forms)</h3>
    <p>Open the PDF in the Mail or Files app, tap the markup icon (pen tip), tap the '+' button, and select Signature. It's fast, but it provides zero legal <a href="/security/audit-trails">Audit Trail</a>.</p>

    <h3>Using usignpdf (Required for business contracts)</h3>
    <p>If you are signing a <a href="/templates/freelance-contract">freelance contract</a> or any legally binding agreement, open Safari, navigate to <a href="/">usignpdf</a>, upload the file, and sign it there. This ensures compliance with the <a href="/legality/us-esign-act">ESIGN Act</a> and <a href="/legality/eu-eidas">eIDAS</a>.</p>
  </div>
